{"base_rate":0.38969616908850724,"brier":0.16912919418758257,"bss":0.2888743444126495,"bss_hi":0.3699014107885274,"bss_lo":0.1900659521368728,"country":"SE","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.11918097754293258,"ess":426.1199852401159,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Uppsala</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Uppsala rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>85%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>7%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 757 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nUPPSALA_AUT, 0.5 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.29, ranked 67 of\n109 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(42&ndash;92) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>7%</b></td><td class='num'>214</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>21%</b></td><td class='num'>86</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>16%</td><td class='num'><b>15%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>37%</td><td class='num'><b>43%</b></td><td class='num'>79</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>67%</td><td class='num'><b>50%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>89%</td><td class='num'><b>63%</b></td><td class='num'>70</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>85%</b></td><td class='num'>157</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Uppsala</b> <span class=\"muted\">SE</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.29</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>42&ndash;92\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 109</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>757 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Uppsala &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Uppsala\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.08271028037383,380.29906542056074 73.35372093023256,348.13953488372096 116.3392,289.78666666666663 190.63797468354431,206.91139240506328 295.92526315789473,99.42105263157896 374.12199999999996,33.599999999999966 411.21082802547767,18.0 411.21082802547767,22.63694267515922 374.12199999999996,85.60000000000002 295.92526315789473,176.05263157894737 190.63797468354431,280.63291139240505 116.3392,352.88 73.35372093023256,377.7674418604651 58.08271028037383,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"240.15059445178338\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"240.15059445178338\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.08271028037383,354.78504672897196 73.35372093023256,305.8139534883721 116.3392,328.61333333333334 190.63797468354431,225.34177215189874 295.92526315789473,200.0 374.12199999999996,153.20000000000002 411.21082802547767,71.32484076433121\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 7% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 214 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.08271028037383\" cy=\"354.78504672897196\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 21% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 86 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"73.35372093023256\" cy=\"305.8139534883721\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 16%&amp;#10;It rained 15% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"116.3392\" cy=\"328.61333333333334\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 37%&amp;#10;It rained 43% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 79 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"190.63797468354431\" cy=\"225.34177215189874\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 67%&amp;#10;It rained 50% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"295.92526315789473\" cy=\"200.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 89%&amp;#10;It rained 63% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 70 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"374.12199999999996\" cy=\"153.20000000000002\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 85% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 157 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.21082802547767\" cy=\"71.32484076433121\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(39%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Uppsala the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.33) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.19).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>42%</td><td class='num'>0.191</td><td class='num'>16.3%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>42%</td><td class='num'>0.268</td><td class='num'>13.5%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>46%</td><td class='num'>0.303</td><td class='num'>12.3%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>28%</td><td class='num'>0.333</td><td class='num'>11.0%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":59.85882,"lon":17.63889,"n":757,"n_cities":109,"name":"Uppsala","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.00023364485981308412,"n